# Gate step 1124-7f3u — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHY IN --check AND NOT ONLY IN --ci-full: this fixture pins the behaviour of
# the PRE-PUSH HOOK, which is the trunk's only gate. A regression in the hook's
# fail-closed rule is not visible from anywhere else — and the defect it pins
# reached trunk precisely because the fast path skipped the check that would
# have caught it. A guard for the gate has to run in the gate.
#
# 267ms measured on lenovinha, hermetic: local bare remote, no network, no
# credentials, and a yq STUB so it cannot skip on a host without yq (this host
# has none, on PATH or via tool-dispatch or in the builder toolbox).
#
# REGIME NOTE (1087-h2z9's lesson, applied before landing rather than after):
# verified on linux/rootless only. No arm uses chmod 000, chown, or any other
# construct root can bypass, so I expect root-parity on the WSL lane — but that
# is an expectation from reading the arms, not a measurement, and it is written
# here as the former.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the plan-only push lane fails closed without a fold validator (1124-7f3u)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-pre-push-plan-lane-fails-closed-without-binary.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the plan-only lane admitted a fragment-bearing push it could not fold, or the fast lane stopped accepting a valid one (1124-7f3u) — see the arm above"
STEP_OK="Plan-lane fail-closed check passed"
